How (the T53 harness): repo copied (no node_modules/.git/.env/.env.*/test-results/.next) into the container, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `pnpm exec prisma generate`, then plain `CI=1 pnpm test:e2e`
  (CI=1 in the container's environment, no --workers flag, so the config's 2 workers). Docker socket mounted from the host, static Docker CLI 27.3.1 (aarch64), TESTCONTAINERS_HOST_OVERRIDE=host.docker.internal
  (--add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway), TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=true (local only). The app server and its throwaway Postgres container come from playwright.config.ts's webServer
  (tests/e2e/support/start-app-server.mjs). .env = env.example with generated AUTH/CRON/LIMIT_KEY secrets and a dummy Sentry DSN; never the repo's .env databases.
  docker run -d --name t58-e2e --ipc=host --init --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway -e TESTCONTAINERS_HOST_OVERRIDE=host.docker.internal -e TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=true \
    -e CI=1 -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock -v <repo copy>:/src:ro mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble sleep infinity; then docker exec for setup and each run. Both runs in the same container and install.

